    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0680" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/11–2849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting ECA Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bissell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-30T20:00:00-05:00">November 30,
                            1949—8 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ecato 1500. [Re] Toeca 2236, sent Taipei (ShaTai 45, rptd Hong Kong Shaeca 451).
                    You are authorized include all raw cotton stocks <pb facs="0681" n="671"
                        xml:id="pg671"/> in overall disposal plans under Allocations Committee of
                    Board Trustees. Are taking necessary action with principals here. Repeated Hong
                    Kong for Nason as Ecato 281 and Taipei as Ecato 211.<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d650-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bissell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d650-f1" n="55" xml:id="d650-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 2359, December 2, 5 p. m., the Department informed the Consul
                    General at Shanghai that telegram Ecato 1500 had been sent with its concurrence
                    (893.50 Recovery/11–2549).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
